This folder contains all preprocessed datasets generated during the ETL pipeline.
Each Approach corresponds to a different machine-learning task, with its own target variable and preprocessing logic.

## Approach 1 — Binary Classification (Hit vs. Non-Hit)
✔ Dataset File Structure
popularity	target_binary	popularity_minmax
6	0	0.06
23	0	0.23
0	0	0.00
57	1	0.57
99	1	0.99
✔ Description

This dataset is built for a binary classification task using a single feature:
popularity (cleaned, validated, range-checked).

Since the original dataset has no target column, a binary label was created:

1 → Hit (popularity > 50)

0 → Non-Hit (popularity ≤ 50)

An additional column is included:

popularity_minmax → Min-Max normalized popularity (0 → 0.0, 100 → 1.0)

Min-Max normalization is optional because the feature already spans a natural 0–100 scale,
but it is included for models or optimizers that perform better on normalized inputs.

## Approach 2 — Multiclass Classification (Popularity Tiers)
✔ Dataset File Structure
popularity	target_multi	popularity_minmax
6	0	0.06
23	0	0.23
0	0	0.00
57	1	0.57
99	3	0.99
✔ Description

This dataset is built for a four-class classification task, again using the cleaned popularity feature.

Since no target label existed in the raw dataset, a tiered popularity category was created:

Popularity Range	Category Name	Encoded Label
0–30	Niche	0
31–60	Average	1
61–80	Popular	2
81–100	Hit / Viral	3

As with Approach 1, a Min-Max normalized version of the feature is also included:

popularity_minmax → scaled to (0, 1)

Normalization is optional but provided for consistency across models and approaches.